# Cloudflare Workers static-assets response headers.
#
# PORT OF vercel.json "headers" — these two files must stay in lockstep for as
# long as the app dual-ships to Vercel and Cloudflare. vercel.json is the
# origin of this content; if you change a header there, change it here too
# (docs/runbooks/cloudflare-migration.md tracks the cutover that retires it).
#
# Workers serves static assets with a default of
#   Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
# so WITHOUT this file every hashed /assets/ bundle revalidates on every load
# and every security header from vercel.json is simply absent. Syntax:
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/headers/

# ── Security headers (every response) ────────────────────────────────────────
# CSP is Report-Only here exactly as on Vercel — it reports violations to
# Sentry without enforcing. Do not promote it to enforcing in this file alone;
# flip both hosts together or the two deployments diverge on a P0 path.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Permissions-Policy: microphone=(), usb=(), serial=(), bluetooth=(), midi=()
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://js.stripe.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com data:; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co wss://*.supabase.co https://*.ingest.us.sentry.io https://*.ingest.sentry.io https://api.stripe.com https://geocoding-api.open-meteo.com https://api.open-meteo.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-src 'self' https://js.stripe.com https://checkout.stripe.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; report-uri https://o4511458803253248.ingest.us.sentry.io/api/4511458819375104/security/?sentry_key=6709c2092ebda9743a803919a79c7b46

# ── Hashed build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vite fingerprints everything under /assets/, so it is immutable by
# construction. public/sw.js depends on this: its hashed-asset branch is
# cache-first precisely because these URLs can never change content.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# ── web-ifc WebAssembly: deliberately NO rule here ───────────────────────────
# vercel.json pins Content-Type: application/wasm on /wasm/. Do NOT port that
# rule — on Cloudflare it makes things worse, verified against `wrangler dev`:
#
#   • Wrangler already derives application/wasm from the .wasm extension when
#     it uploads the asset, so a REAL /wasm/web-ifc.wasm is correctly typed
#     with no rule at all.
#   • A path-pattern rule also applies to the SPA fallback. With "/wasm/*  ->
#     Content-Type: application/wasm", a request for a /wasm/ path that does
#     NOT exist returned 200 with index.html in the body labelled
#     application/wasm — WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming then fails on a
#     confusing compile error instead of a clean 404.
#
# The IFC viewer renders zero geometry with no error on a wrong MIME type, so
# the failure this rule would cause is exactly the one it looks like it
# prevents. Leave it out.

# ── Preview URLs must never be indexed ───────────────────────────────────────
# Vercel preview deployments were auth-walled by the platform; Cloudflare
# *.workers.dev preview URLs are PUBLIC by default. The app still gates data
# behind Supabase auth, but the shell should not be crawlable. Cloudflare
# Access is the real fix — see the runbook. This is the cheap backstop.
https://:version.:subdomain.workers.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
